From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:32:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] rockchip: bootrom: a stage loaded over USB does not go
 back for the download flag

Copyright (C) 2026 Olympian LED, Inc.

The BootROM never reads the download flag (BOOT_BROM_DOWNLOAD in the
boot-mode register); the stage it boots does, and goes back to the
BootROM's download mode. The flag is still in the register when the
BootROM is in that mode: whoever wrote it (a loader's Rockusb `RD 3`)
reset into it. So a TPL or SPL sent over USB from there found its own
request served, cleared the flag and went straight back: the BootROM
waited for the same download again and the host's download failed.
Only a second download, the flag cleared, would boot.

Honor the flag only when the stage was not loaded over USB: when the
BootROM's boot-source word does not read 10 (USB), nor 0x81, the value
read_brom_bootsource_id() maps to USB. The flag is cleared either way.
Rockchip's own RK3399 loader (rkbin rk3399_ddr_800MHz_v1.30), sent over
USB from the same state, boots as well.

Safe without a switch: a boot from the card reads the card's
boot-source word (2 eMMC, 5 SD), never USB, so it honors the flag
exactly as before; only a stage that came over USB, which the flag's
request already got there, carries on.

Signed-off-by: Brady <brady@aioscilloscope.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/bootrom.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/bootrom.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/bootrom.c
index 1db38546..107b726b 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/bootrom.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/bootrom.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2017 Google, Inc
  */
 
+#include <config.h>
 #include <hang.h>
 #include <setjmp.h>
 #include <asm/arch-rockchip/bootrom.h>
@@ -51,6 +52,17 @@ static bool check_back_to_brom_dnl_flag(void)
 		boot_mode = readl(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG);
 		if (boot_mode == BOOT_BROM_DOWNLOAD) {
 			writel(0, CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG);
+			/*
+			 * Loaded over USB, this stage was sent by the BootROM's download mode: the flag
+			 * that put the BootROM there is served (the flag stays in the register through
+			 * that reset, the BootROM never reads it). Going back would only make the BootROM
+			 * wait for this same download again. A stage booted from the card still goes back,
+			 * as before; only one whose boot-source word reads USB (10, or 0x81) carries on.
+			 */
+			if (BROM_BOOTSOURCE_ID_ADDR &&
+			    (readl(BROM_BOOTSOURCE_ID_ADDR) == BROM_BOOTSOURCE_USB ||
+			     readl(BROM_BOOTSOURCE_ID_ADDR) == 0x81))
+				return false;
 			return true;
 		}
 	}
